    <div class="hwaet-project-intro">
      <p>
        A standalone short film adapted from the first act of the planned
        feature film, <em>Drag Me to Winchester</em>, following a medieval
        charcoal burner through a three-day charcoal burn in the New Forest
        towards his destined discovery of the dead body of King William Rufus.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>


  <section class="hwaet-project-content">

    <h2 class="hwaet-section-title">The Film</h2>

    <p class="hwaet-series-intro">
      Set in the New Forest in 1100, <em>Earthburn</em> follows Purkiss,
      a charcoal burner living and working in the forest in the days
      immediately before the death of King William II.
    </p>

  </section>


  <section class="hwaet-project-content hwaet-series-two">

    <h2 class="hwaet-section-title">Production</h2>

    <p>
      Filmed on the Beaulieu Estate in the New Forest, <em>Earthburn</em> features
      a charcoal making method (a pit kiln) which seems not to have been attempted
      for nearly 600 years. In consultation with local craftspeople and historians we
      performed the pit burn in conjunction with the film shoot.  
    </p>

  </section>


